# Store & sync

## Orchestration

All unlock / pull / push / conflict / password / import flows go through `useTandemStore`. Preserve optimistic SHA locking in `pushRemoteVault`.

## Conflicts

On `GitHubConflictError`, set `conflict` (include `summary` from `summarizeVaultConflict` when remote ciphertext decrypts) and let `ConflictDialog` choose **pull** or **overwrite**. No silent merge of `history` months.

Conflict **pull** must clear `localDirty` (and `conflict`) before `pull()` — a dirty-first re-push would recreate the same conflict and leave the dialog stuck.

## Quiet pull

`pull({ quiet: true })` (visibility/focus + unlock background): never auto-push; no-op when dirty/syncing/conflicted; swallow network errors. Manual header pull still pushes dirty first.

## Vault file

Path is always `tandem_data.json.enc` (`DATA_FILENAME`). Branch default `main`.

## Session restore

Quiet unlock may use session vault cache then background-fetch. Don’t break offline-tolerant refresh.

## Settings caveat

`updateState` sets `localDirty` until successful `push` / pull apply. Pull (header sync) pushes first when dirty. Background unlock refresh must skip while `localDirty`. Prefer **Save & sync** after Settings edits; lock still drops unsynced memory.

## Initial state

`createInitialState()` defaults to **empty** history (C3A). Opt in with `withDemoData: true` or Settings → `loadDemoData`. Setup / empty-remote unlock must keep empty vaults.
